# Repos a reviewer of THIS repo may search and cite, materialized under
# .siblings/<owner>/<repo>. Declared rather than left to the fallback so the
# set is the one this repo actually depends on.
#
# One per line. The reviewer host must also carry a SOURCE_PATHS entry for
# each, or the sibling reports as `missing` and is never searched.
#
# Each row is a real edge. `latch` owns the MCP tools and the gog grammar that
# research, calendar, mail and print drive. `plow-wiki` is the wiki the paper
# writes, and its schema and CLI are the contract the wiki scripts follow.
# `agent-index-client` is the reporter the Dockerfile fetches by sha.
# `plow-agents` owns the install contract. `plow-openclaw-agent` is the
# OpenClaw base this repo's `boot/` duplicates. It is listed so a reviewer can
# tell when boot logic already exists there.
#
# `plow-pbc/plow` stays out although the scripts call its API: it is private
# and this repo is public, so a citation into it would publish private paths.

plow-pbc/latch
plow-pbc/plow-wiki
plow-pbc/agent-index-client
plow-pbc/plow-agents
plow-pbc/plow-openclaw-agent
